WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.080
Every strand of DNA has a
direction, like an arrow.

2
00:00:04.130 --> 00:00:07.440
It has a 5 prime end and a 3 prime end.

3
00:00:07.490 --> 00:00:11.600
In a double helix, the two strands
run in opposite directions.

4
00:00:11.650 --> 00:00:16.590
And DNA polymerase adds nucleotides
only at the 3 prime end.

5
00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:19.370
A new strand grows one way only.

6
00:00:19.420 --> 00:00:24.070
So when the helix opens, how can
both strands be copied at once?

7
00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:28.300
In this mission, you'll number the carbons
of a sugar to see where those two ends

8
00:00:28.350 --> 00:00:29.480
come from.

9
00:00:29.530 --> 00:00:32.570
Then you'll stand at a
replication fork as it opens,

10
00:00:32.620 --> 00:00:35.710
and work out how each new strand is built.

11
00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:40.440
Your mission: explain how both
strands of DNA are copied at once.
